        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Rubio faces challenge in Pope Leo meeting after Trump's criticism over Iran Issued on: 07/05/2026 - 11:44 Modified: 07/05/2026 - 11:44 America's top diplomat, Marco Rubio, will meet the first US pope, Leo XIV, on Thursday, seeking to ease Washington-Vatican tensions while also promoting President Donald Trump's agenda. The US secretary of state arrived in Rome after Trump's extraordinary criticism of Leo, the head of the world's 1.4 billion Catholics, over his anti-war stance. FRANCE 24's Hannah Roberts reports from Rome, Italy. US Rubio seeks to ease tensions with US pope after Trump's attacks 07/05/2026 Trump sees swift end to war as Iran reviews US peace proposal 07/05/2026 UK voters cast ballots in elections expected to deal blow to Starmer 07/05/2026 What to know about hantavirus, the illness linked to a cruise ship outbreak 07/05/2026 Argentina probes link to deadly hantavirus outbreak on Atlantic cruise 07/05/2026 Holders PSG edge Bayern Munich to reach Champions League final 07/05/2026 Cruise ship with hantavirus outbreak heads to Spain's Canary Islands after 3 are evacuated 07/05/2026 Britons set to punish Starmer's Labour in local polls 07/05/2026 Stitching lives back together for Central African Republic's child soldiers 07/05/2026"
